<title>GERMANY: German Q3 GDP rises 1.0 pct q/q, 2.4 pct y/y.</title>
<headline>German Q3 GDP rises 1.0 pct q/q, 2.4 pct y/y.</headline>
<dateline>WIESBADEN, Germany 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Statistics Office reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p>PAN-GERMAN GDP     Q3 96	 Q2 96	  Q1 96</p>
<p> qtr/qtr	     +1.0	   +1.5	   -0.5</p>
<p> yr/yr		 +2.4	   +1.2	   +0.2</p>
<p>W.GERMAN GDP</p>
<p> yr/yr		 +2.2	   +1.0	    n/a</p>
<p>E.GERMAN GDP</p>
<p> yr/yr		 +4.1	   +3.0	    n/a</p>
<p>NOTE - Quarter-on-quarter figures are adjusted for inflation (1991 prices) and for seasonal and calendar factors. They are rounded to a half pct point. Yr/yr changes are adjusted for inflation but not seasonal or calendar factors.  </p>
<p>The Office gave the following yr/yr details:</p>
<p>PAN-GERMAN GDP	     Q3 96	 Q2 96</p>
<p> Private consumption     +1.6	  +0.9</p>
<p> Public consumption	+3.3	  +2.8</p>
<p> Capital investment	+3.2	  +2.1</p>
<p> Construction		+1.6	  -1.6</p>
<p> Exports		     +5.9	  +2.1</p>
<p> Imports		     +2.0	  +0.3</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
</text>
